{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would represent a bulky and visually obtrusive addition that would harm the living conditions of the neighbouring residents on Burns Avenue and Harlington Road West through an overbearing impact, loss of outlook and privacy. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policies D3, D4 and Policy CC2 of the Local Plan and the NPPF.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development would give rise to significant highways and transport impacts to the detriment of road safety and the free flow of traffic therefore failing to comply with London Plan Policies T4, T6, T6.1, T7, EC2 and Policy EQ7 of the Local Plan and the NPPF",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development has not demonstrated good living conditions for future residents as it would not provide suitable communal amenity space (quality and quantum) therefore failing to comply with London Plan Policies D4, D5, D6 and Policies SC3, SC4, SC5 of the Local Plan and the NPPF",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed development has failed to demonstrate that the drainage strategy is in accordance with London Plan Policies SI12 and SI13 and Policy EQ3 of the Local Plan and the NPPF",
    "Reason : 5 - In the absence of a signed legal agreement to secure a Carbon Offset Fund contribution, the application is therefore contrary to Local Plan Policy IMP3"
  ],
